Testing that the hardware offload flowtable lists each configured wireless
interface of a zone network, present in sysfs or not: an AP with its WDS
port prefix, another mode by name, and a wifi-vlan by the name that the
status reports or, if it has a VLAN ID, by <ifname>-<name>. An interface
of a disabled radio, of a network outside the zones, without a name, or
with a name too long for a hook or with a character that a hook cannot
take is left out, and so is a name or a prefix under another listed prefix,
because the kernel refuses such a list. A radio that waits for its CAC keeps
its interfaces. Entries of the status that are not objects are skipped.

